<td id="S5.T4.8.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">24.7</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T4.8.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T4.8.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T4.8.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen2.5-VL-7B</span></td>
<td id="S5.T4.8.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">19.8</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T4.8.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T4.8.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">   + <span id="S5.T4.8.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">SciMDR</span></td>
<td id="S5.T4.8.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">49.1<span id="S5.T4.8.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"><sup id="S5.T4.8.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.T4.8.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#8B0000;">+29.3</span></sup></span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Baselines. ‣ 5.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ SciMDR: Benchmarking and Advancing Scientific Multimodal Document Reasoning" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 3</span></a>presents the comparative performance of model fine-tuned with <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SciMDR</span>, against the baselines across all four benchmarks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results substantiate the efficacy of our approach (RQ1). <em id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Model fine-tuned with <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SciMDR</span> achieves substantial improvements over the base model across the board</em>, effectively transforming a general-purpose multimodal model into a specialized scientific assistant.
To further contextualize the difficulty of our proposed benchmark and the effectiveness of our method, we compare our fine-tuned model against advanced proprietary models on <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SciMDR</span>-Eval. Despite its smaller parameter size 7B, model with <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SciMDR</span> exhibits competitive performance on this scientific reasoning task.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Pipeline Effectiveness and Analysis</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Having established the performance gains, we address RQ2 by analyzing the quality of our synthetic data and deconstructing the contributions of our pipeline components.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Data Quality Comparison</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess the quality of our synthetic data independent of the base model’s intrinsic capabilities, we conduct a controlled comparison using <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LLaVA-1.5-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2024b)</a></cite>.
We chose <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LLaVA-1.5</span> as our probing model for two strategic reasons: its fully transparent training data ensures no prior exposure to our evaluation benchmarks, and as a more modest baseline, it is more sensitive to data quality, allowing us to clearly observe the marginal gains from different instruction-tuning datasets.
We fine-tune <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LLaVA-1.5-7B</span> on three configurations: (1) 50K samples from SPIQA, (2) 50K VQA samples from <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SciMDR</span>, and (3) 50K samples from SPIQA re-annotated using our claim-centric pipeline. All models are trained for 2 epochs and evaluated on on single-image benchmarks to match the model’s input constraint.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span><span id="S5.T5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Controlled data quality comparison.</span> The results based on <span id="S5.T5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">LLaVA-1.5-7B</span> show that re-annotating SPIQA’s source documents with our pipeline yields improvements over the original labels, confirming the superiority of our generation methodology.</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T5.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.T5.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ChartQA</span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CharXiv</span></td>
<td id="S5.T5.6.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T5.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SPIQA-A</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T5.6.2" class="ltx_tr">
