<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span><span id="A3.F5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim extraction prompt.</span> This prompt guides the LLM to distill paragraphs into structured, verifiable claims serving as blueprints for QA generation.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F6.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1700.05" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 1700.05" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1700.05) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 1695.42 C 0 1697.98 2.07 1700.05 4.63 1700.05 L 648.52 1700.05 C 651.08 1700.05 653.15 1697.98 653.15 1695.42 L 653.15 4.63 C 653.15 2.07 651.08 0 648.52 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 1695.42 C 0.69 1697.6 2.45 1699.36 4.63 1699.36 L 648.52 1699.36 C 650.7 1699.36 652.46 1697.6 652.46 1695.42 L 652.46 4.63 C 652.46 2.45 650.7 0.69 648.52 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 204.76)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:107.16em;--ltx-fo-depth:13.89em;font-size:10pt;" height="1675.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 1482.81)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System:<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> You are a meticulous Multimodal Analyst and Fact-Checker. Your expertise is in precisely matching textual claims with visual evidence.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Your mission is to receive structured textual claims (JSON format) and, for <span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">each claim</span>, systematically find corresponding visual evidence within a given image and caption. You will annotate findings by adding a <span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">visual_grounding</span> field to each object.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Inputs<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. <span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Structured Textual Claims (JSON):</span> {text_json}</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. <span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Caption:</span> {caption}</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Process<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For <span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">each claim object</span>, strictly follow this procedure:</span></span>
<span id="A3.I8" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A3.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A3.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I8.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Analyze the Claim</span><span id="A3.I8.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Read the claim’s </span><span id="A3.I8.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">content</span><span id="A3.I8.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><span id="A3.I8.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">key_entities</span><span id="A3.I8.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to understand its core assertion.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A3.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I8.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Locate Visual Elements</span><span id="A3.I8.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Search the image and caption for relevant visual elements (e.g., lines in a graph, bars in a chart, labels, specific regions, or text).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I8.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A3.I8.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I8.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I8.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Critically Evaluate the Evidence</span><span id="A3.I8.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Is the visual element </span><span id="A3.I8.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">directly</span><span id="A3.I8.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><span id="A3.I8.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">explicitly</span><span id="A3.I8.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> related to the claim? Thematic relevance alone is insufficient. If evidence exists, determine its nature: Does it support, quantify, illustrate, or contradict the claim?</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I8.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<span id="A3.I8.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Construct the <span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">visual_grounding</span> Object</span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: If you </span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">cannot find</span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> direct visual evidence, construct </span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{"exists_in_visual": false}</span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. If you </span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">find</span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> direct evidence, construct a complete object with </span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"exists_in_visual": true</span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> along with </span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">relationship_type</span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">visual_element_description</span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">justification</span><span id="A3.I8.i4.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output Requirements<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.9.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Output a single, complete, augmented JSON object. Ensure the original JSON’s structure is fully preserved. The only modification should be the addition of the <span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">visual_grounding</span> field to every original claim object.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">visual_grounding<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> Field Definitions<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.I9" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A3.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I9.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">exists_in_visual</span><span id="A3.I9.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: (Boolean) Required. </span><span id="A3.I9.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">true</span><span id="A3.I9.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> if direct visual evidence is found, otherwise </span><span id="A3.I9.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">false</span><span id="A3.I9.i1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I9.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">relationship_type</span><span id="A3.I9.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: (String) Required if </span><span id="A3.I9.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">exists_in_visual</span><span id="A3.I9.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is </span><span id="A3.I9.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">true</span><span id="A3.I9.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Must be one of: [”Supports”, ”Quantifies”, ”Illustrates”, ”Elaborates”, ”Contradicts”].</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I9.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I9.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I9.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I9.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">visual_element_description</span><span id="A3.I9.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: (String) Required if </span><span id="A3.I9.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">exists_in_visual</span><span id="A3.I9.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is </span><span id="A3.I9.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">true</span><span id="A3.I9.i3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. A clear, textual description of the relevant visual element(s).</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I9.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I9.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I9.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I9.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">justification</span><span id="A3.I9.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: (String) Required if </span><span id="A3.I9.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">exists_in_visual</span><span id="A3.I9.i4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is </span><span id="A3.I9.i4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">true</span><span id="A3.I9.i4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. A detailed explanation of how the visual element is linked to the textual claim.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">relationship_type<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif"> Definitions<span id="A3.F6.pic1.1.12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.I10" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A3.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I10.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Supports</span><span id="A3.I10.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Visual evidence directly confirms or strengthens the assertion.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I10.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Quantifies</span><span id="A3.I10.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Visual evidence provides specific numerical data or measurements.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I10.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I10.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I10.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I10.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Illustrates</span><span id="A3.I10.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Visual evidence provides a visual example or representation.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I10.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I10.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I10.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I10.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Elaborates</span><span id="A3.I10.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Visual evidence provides additional details or context.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I10.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I10.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I10.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I10.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Contradicts</span><span id="A3.I10.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Visual evidence directly refutes or opposes the assertion.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span><span id="A3.F6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Visual grounding prompt.</span> This prompt matches textual claims with visual evidence, determining relationship types (Supports, Quantifies, Illustrates, Elaborates, Contradicts).</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1429.31" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 1429.31" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1429.31) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 1424.68 C 0 1427.24 2.07 1429.31 4.63 1429.31 L 648.52 1429.31 C 651.08 1429.31 653.15 1427.24 653.15 1424.68 L 653.15 4.63 C 653.15 2.07 651.08 0 648.52 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 1424.68 C 0.69 1426.85 2.45 1428.62 4.63 1428.62 L 648.52 1428.62 C 650.7 1428.62 652.46 1426.85 652.46 1424.68 L 652.46 4.63 C 652.46 2.45 650.7 0.69 648.52 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:101.3em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="1404.32" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 1401.63)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System:<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> You are an expert AI Research Assistant specializing in multimodal scientific reasoning. Your goal is to generate challenging, high-quality multimodal questions for each claim with visual grounding.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question Categories<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. Evidence-Based Explanation &amp; Quantification (EEQ)<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Core: Explain HOW and WHY a visual element supports a textual claim, and quantify that support. Example: ”The authors claim that [statement]. How exactly does the data in [Figure/Table X] support this claim, and can you quantify the effect?”</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. Concept-to-Instance Mapping (CIM)<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Core: Link an abstract concept, architecture, or process described in text to its concrete visual representation. Example: ”The paper defines ’[concept]’ in Section X. Identify the corresponding components in [Figure Y] and explain how they match the description.”</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. Hypothesis Validation &amp; Inferential Reasoning (HVI)<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Core: Use combined evidence from text and visuals to validate a hypothesis, infer conclusions, or predict outcomes. Example: ”The hypothesis is that [hypothesis]. How do the results in [Figure X], combined with the text’s interpretation, validate this hypothesis?”</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. Critical Analysis &amp; Consistency Check (CAC)<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.9.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Core: Critically evaluate whether textual claims are accurately supported by visual data. Example: ”The text describes the improvement in [Figure X] as ’significant’. Based on the visual evidence and scale, is this characterization accurate?”</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5. Argumentative Role &amp; Synthesis (ARS)<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.11.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Core: Summarize the overall scientific takeaway and the specific role of visual evidence in the paper’s main argument. Example: ”What is the core scientific takeaway from the combination of [Figure X] and its description in the text?”</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.13.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For each claim, generate one question requiring deep, integrated understanding of THREE sources: (1) Figure/Table image, (2) Caption, (3) Context text. The question MUST NOT be answerable by looking at only one or two sources in isolation.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Inputs<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.15.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. <span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Verified Textual Claims:</span> {claims_json}</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. <span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Context:</span> {context}</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. <span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Caption:</span> {caption}</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Guiding Philosophy<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.19.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Think Like a Scientist, Not a Grader. Your primary goal is to frame questions from the perspective of a curious scientist trying to understand the <em id="A3.F7.pic1.1.20.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">phenomenon</em>, not a teacher asking a student to interpret a chart. The question should be about the ’what’, ’why’, or ’how’ of the scientific concept itself. The text and visual are simply the <em id="A3.F7.pic1.1.20.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">resources</em> the user needs to construct the answer.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Methodology: 4-Step Chain of Thought<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.21.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 1: Deep Analysis &amp; Synthesis<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.22.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.23.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Review all claims. What is the central scientific story they tell with the visual? Analyze the visual, caption, and context. Identify key relationships, trends, and mechanisms. Synthesize sources to form a high-level understanding.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.24" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.24.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 2: Strategic Question Type Selection<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.24.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.25" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.25.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Based on synthesis, choose the MOST appropriate question sub-type (EEQ, CIM, HVI, CAC, or ARS) that would lead to a challenging and insightful question.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.26" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.26.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 3: Draft the Final Multimodal Question<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.26.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.27" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.27.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Core Principle<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.27.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Ask about the concept, not the evidence. Frame the question around the scientific idea, process, or implication. The user will naturally have to find the evidence in the provided materials.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.28" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.28.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Crucially, re-examine your question using these examples:<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.28.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.I11" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A3.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I11.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">BAD</span><span id="A3.I11.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: ”How does the diagram illustrate that you must visit all target regions?”</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I11.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">GOOD</span><span id="A3.I11.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: ”Why must all potential target regions be searched before the target’s precise location can be confirmed?”</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.29" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.29.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Use Diverse Framing Strategies<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.29.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">:</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.I12" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A3.I12.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I12.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I12.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I12.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Causal Reasoning (Why?): ”What is the primary reason for the observed drop in efficiency when temperature exceeds 50°C?”</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I12.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I12.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I12.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I12.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Procedural Understanding (How?): ”If a new data point were introduced, walk through the steps the algorithm would take to classify it.”</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I12.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I12.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I12.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I12.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Hypothetical Scenarios (What if?): ”What would be the likely impact if the ’attention’ module were removed?”</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I12.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I12.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I12.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I12.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Defining Conditions (Under what…): ”For which demographic does the interface show the most significant usability improvement?”</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I12.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I12.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I12.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I12.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Integrative Synthesis (What implication?): ”What is the overarching conclusion regarding system stability when combining error rates in Table 1 with the risk assessment in the conclusion?”</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I12.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<span id="A3.I12.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I12.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I12.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Critical Discrepancy (What inconsistency?): ”What specific data behaviors contradict the author’s claim of a ’linear relationship’?”</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.30" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.30.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Check<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.30.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Read aloud. Does it sound natural? It must not contain words like ”figure,” ”table,” ”diagram,” ”graph,” or ”according to the text.”</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.31" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.31.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step 4: Generate a Conclusive Answer<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.31.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.32" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F7.pic1.1.32.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Provide a comprehensive, step-by-step answer. Your reasoning must explicitly cite evidence from the visual, caption, and context. When describing visual information, meticulously detail all relevant visual elements and explicitly connect them to the question.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span><span id="A3.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MQA generation prompt.</span> This prompt generates questions requiring synthesis of textual and visual information across five reasoning types (EEQ, CIM, HVI, CAC, ARS).</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F8.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="988.75" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 988.75" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,988.75) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#606060;" fill="#606060" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 984.12 C 0 986.68 2.07 988.75 4.63 988.75 L 648.52 988.75 C 651.08 988.75 653.15 986.68 653.15 984.12 L 653.15 4.63 C 653.15 2.07 651.08 0 648.52 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 984.12 C 0.69 986.3 2.45 988.06 4.63 988.06 L 648.52 988.06 C 650.7 988.06 652.46 986.3 652.46 984.12 L 652.46 4.63 C 652.46 2.45 650.7 0.69 648.52 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:69.4em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="963.76" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 960.3)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System:<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> You are an expert Visual Question-Answering pair generator. Your task is to analyze a provided image context (e.g., chart, graph, table) and a specified question category to create a structured JSON object.</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question Categories<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.I13" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A3.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A3.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I13.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">DR, Data Retrieval (Lookup)</span><span id="A3.I13.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Asks for a specific data point that can be directly read from the image.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A3.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I13.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">EI, Extremum Identification (Max/Min)</span><span id="A3.I13.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Asks to find the highest, lowest, largest, or smallest value, or the entity associated with it.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I13.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A3.I13.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I13.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I13.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">CO, Computation</span><span id="A3.I13.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Requires a mathematical calculation (e.g., sum, difference, average, percentage change) based on data points from the image.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I13.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<span id="A3.I13.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I13.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I13.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">CT, Counting</span><span id="A3.I13.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Requires counting the number of elements that meet a specific numerical criterion.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I13.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<span id="A3.I13.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I13.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I13.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">CR, Comparison &amp; Ranking</span><span id="A3.I13.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Requires comparing two or more data points or finding an entity with a specific rank.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I13.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<span id="A3.I13.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I13.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I13.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">TP, Trend &amp; Pattern Analysis</span><span id="A3.I13.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Focuses on overall behavior of data over time, correlations, or specific patterns.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I13.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">7.</span> 
<span id="A3.I13.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I13.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I13.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">IP, Inference &amp; Prediction</span><span id="A3.I13.i7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Asks for a projection, estimation based on a trend, or hypothetical outcome.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I13.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">8.</span> 
<span id="A3.I13.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I13.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I13.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">MS, Compositional Reasoning (Multi-Step)</span><span id="A3.I13.i8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: A complex question that requires combining two or more of the above types.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Task<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Based on the provided image context and the specified question category, generate one QA pair.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question Category:<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Choose the MOST appropriate question sub-type that would lead to a challenging and insightful question. {VISUAL_ONLY_QUESTION_CATEGORY}</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Caption:<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> {caption}</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Rules<span id="A3.F8.pic1.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.I14" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<span id="A3.I14.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<span id="A3.I14.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I14.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I14.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question Generation</span><span id="A3.I14.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: The generated question must be relevant to the specified category and must be answerable </span><em id="A3.I14.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">solely</em><span id="A3.I14.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> by analyzing the visual information in the image context.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I14.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<span id="A3.I14.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I14.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I14.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Global Image Description</span><span id="A3.I14.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: First, give a comprehensive and detailed description of what you see in the image. Describe the type of visualization, its main components, labels, colors, layout, values, the magnitude and positional relationships of values of each element, and any important visual elements.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I14.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<span id="A3.I14.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I14.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I14.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Relevant Parts of Image</span><span id="A3.I14.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Connect the image description to the specific question being asked. Identify which parts of the image are relevant to answering the question.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I14.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<span id="A3.I14.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I14.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I14.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Step-by-Step Reasoning</span><span id="A3.I14.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Provide step-by-step reasoning to find the answer. Each step should build on the previous one.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I14.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<span id="A3.I14.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I14.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I14.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer</span><span id="A3.I14.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: State the final answer clearly in a single, complete sentence.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I14.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<span id="A3.I14.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I14.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I14.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Short Form Answer</span><span id="A3.I14.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Provide a concise version of the answer, typically a number, word, or short phrase, suitable for automated evaluation.</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.I14.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">7.</span> 
<span id="A3.I14.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.I14.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I14.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">JSON Structure</span><span id="A3.I14.i7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">: Your final output MUST be a single, raw JSON object strictly adhering to the following structure.</span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
